x":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State in Context that `resolve_plan_review_engine` currently performs no `.strip()`/`.lower()` normalization (cite the comparison line), or state the fallback if it does (drop the whitespace case vs. allow a source change).","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E2","COH","T2"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.6,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Context: 'no test pins that the comparison is case-sensitive'. Whitespace is not mentioned.","Approach: 'calls `resolve_plan_review_engine` with `\"Agentic\"`, `\"PIPELINE\"` and `\" pipeline\"` ... No source change'","Whether the function normalizes input with `.strip()` is a load-bearing codebase fact that the plan does not state."],"finding":"The plan assumes `resolve_plan_review_engine` already rejects `\" pipeline\"` (a leading space) and also commits to 'No source change'. Nothing establishes that the current implementation does not strip whitespace. If it does strip, AC2 cannot be met without breaking the stated no-source-change constraint. The Context section only argues the case-sensitivity gap ('no test pins that the comparison is case-sensitive'); it says nothing about whitespace.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc67490e161f5c11c","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Context / Problem vs Approach (\" pipeline\" input; 'No source change')","norm_id":"n03ac491340a47d93","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The implementation calls `engine.strip()` before the membership check. The `\" pipeline\"` case then passes resolution and does not raise, so the test fails and the executor must choose between editing source (out of scope) and dropping the case."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add one sentence to Context: 'The check is a plain `engine not in PLAN_REVIEW_ENGINES` with no normalization, so all three values already raise.' Also add: 'If whitespace is found to be stripped, remove `\" pipeline\"` from the parametrization rather than changing source.'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2222,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"no","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"yes","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the default assertion form: `with pytest.raises(ConfigError) as exc: ...; assert value in str(exc.value)` (or `match=re.escape(value)`).","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E2"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.567,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'asserts each raises `rebar.config.ConfigError` whose message names the rejected value'","No assertion mechanism is stated."],"finding":"The plan does not say how the 'message names the rejected value' assertion is made. For `\" pipeline\"`, using `pytest.raises(..., match=value)` treats the value as a regex, and a message that renders the value via repr (`' pipeline'`) could make a naive check behave unexpectedly. This is a defaultable gap the plan should settle by stating a default.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb403d20c9566cc1b","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / AC1 ('asserting `ConfigError` with the value in its message')","norm_id":"n1ec8872f770143f8","priority":0.033,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The executor uses `match=value` without `re.escape`, or checks the stripped form. The leading-space case then does not truly verify the rejected value."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Specify `assert value in str(excinfo.value)` as the message check.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.125,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Make the ticket's disposition unambiguous: either mark it not-ready/do-not-implement in status, or drop the 'not intended to be implemented' line so the ACs are authoritative.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E2","COH"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.534,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Preamble: 'its plan is not intended to be implemented'","Acceptance Criteria: two unchecked `- [ ]` items describing implementation work."],"finding":"The plan sends mixed signals about whether it should be carried out. The preamble says the ticket 'will be closed as obsolete afterwards and its plan is not intended to be implemented'. The Approach, Scope and ACs, however, are written as a fully implementable spec with checkbox criteria. An executing agent would have to ask whether to do the work.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f82f08b7c167f8d61","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Preamble vs Approach / Acceptance Criteria","norm_id":"n3132a80d20cda0c3","priority":0.066,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An agent picks the ticket up from a ready queue and either implements throwaway work or stalls on the contradiction."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] In Context, state that explicit engine names are intentionally exact (case- and whitespace-sensitive), give the reason (e.g. consistency with config-file validation via `_as_choice`), and confirm the current implementation does no stripping or case normalization.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.net-mechanism","project.portability"],"criteria":["E5","E3"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Context: \"no test pins that the comparison is case-sensitive\". Whitespace is never mentioned.","Approach: \"calls `resolve_plan_review_engine` with `\"Agentic\"`, `\"PIPELINE\"` and `\" pipeline\"`\" and \"No source change\".","Test name `test_explicit_engine_is_case_and_whitespace_sensitive` asserts a whitespace contract that the plan never establishes or justifies."],"finding":"The new test pins whitespace-sensitivity (`\" pipeline\"`) and case-sensitivity as the contract of `resolve_plan_review_engine`. The plan never says this is the intended contract rather than current behaviour. Context only claims the comparison is case-sensitive and says nothing about whitespace handling. Because the plan also says 'No source change' and requires the suite to exit 0, it silently depends on the function doing no `.strip()` or `.lower()` today. If any such normalization exists, the AC is unsatisfiable as written. If neither property is intended, the test becomes a change-detector that locks in incidental behaviour.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fcccfbcd329ed8459","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Context / Problem and Approach; Acceptance Criteria line 1","norm_id":"nd41b8d0b4b12c5fb","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The function already strips its input. The `\" pipeline\"` case resolves to `pipeline`, the test fails, and AC 2 cannot pass without a source change the plan rules out.","A future deliberate decision to accept `\"Pipeline\"` would be blocked by a test that never documented why exactness is required."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2222,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"no","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"yes","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.75,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Correct the out-of-scope note: `_as_choice` lives in src/rebar/_config_coercion.py (used from _config_sections.py) and strips and lower-cases config values. Then state explicitly that the explicit argument is meant to be stricter than the config key, or reconsider pinning strictness.","cohort":["E4"],"criteria":["E4"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.5667,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: \"Out of scope: config-file values (already validated by `_as_choice` in `src/rebar/_config_sections.py`).\"","Plan: \"a change that lower-cased the argument would go unnoticed\"","src/rebar/_config_coercion.py:232-236: `def _as_choice(v, key, choices): s = str(v).strip().lower(); if s not in choices: raise ConfigError(...); return s`","src/rebar/_config_sections.py:8 imports `_as_choice`; line 58: `\"plan_review_engine\": lambda v, k: _as_choice(v, k, {\"pipeline\", \"agentic\"})`","src/rebar/llm/plan_review/__init__.py:310: `if engine not in PLAN_REVIEW_ENGINES:` (no normalization)"],"finding":"The out-of-scope claim leans on a premise the code contradicts. It says config-file values are 'already validated by `_as_choice` in `src/rebar/_config_sections.py`', which implies they get the same strict check. In fact `_as_choice` is defined in src/rebar/_config_coercion.py and runs `str(v).strip().lower()` before checking. So `plan_review_engine = \"Agentic\"` or `\" pipeline\"` in rebar.toml is accepted and normalized, not rejected. The plan treats lower-casing the explicit argument as a regression to guard against, yet the config path already lower-cases. The new test would lock in a mismatch between the two paths without saying so.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f1ca3e4310d589038","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"## Scope — Out of scope: config-file values (already validated by `_as_choice` in `src/rebar/_config_sections.py`)","norm_id":"n0b4fca06066adcba","priority":0.1833,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reader takes the exclusion to mean config values are case-strict too. But rebar.toml `plan_review_engine = \"Agentic\"` loads fine while `review_plan(engine=\"Agentic\")` raises ConfigError, and nothing in the plan or tests documents this mismatch.","A later maintainer sees the case-insensitive config path, 'fixes' the explicit path to match, and the new test then fails with no recorded reason why strictness was intended."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Reword the exclusion to: \"Out of scope: config-file values — validated by `_as_choice` (src/rebar/_config_coercion.py, applied in src/rebar/_config_sections.py:58), which strips and lower-cases before checking, so `\\\"Agentic\\\"` in rebar.toml is accepted as `agentic`. The explicit argument is intentionally stricter; this test pins that difference.\"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.3333,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"no","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"incomplete_enumeration","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add a proving command for AC1 that collects the named test and asserts exactly 3 parametrized items.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.6062,"drop_reason":"novelty","evidence":["AC1: 'parametrized over `\"Agentic\"`, `\"PIPELINE\"` and `\" pipeline\"`'","Testing: only 'Run `.venv/bin/pytest tests/unit/test_plan_review_engine_switch.py -q`'","Verify-command taxonomy item (5): missing cardinality assertion when the criterion names a count."],"finding":"AC1 is structural: the test exists, is parametrized over three values, and asserts the value appears in the message. AC2's only proving command is a whole-file `pytest -q` exit 0. That still passes if the test is missing, mis-named, has fewer parameters, or omits the message assertion. No command checks the stated count of three cases.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fa7b26dea898aa5b7","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria, AC1 / Testing","norm_id":"nb2e89333eaac4cac","priority":0.3438,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The executor adds only two parameters, or names the test differently. The file run is still green, so AC2 is satisfied while AC1 is not."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"`.venv/bin/pytest tests/unit/test_plan_review_engine_switch.py -q --collect-only -k test_explicit_engine_is_case_and_whitespace_sensitive | grep -c '::test_explicit_engine_is_case_and_whitespace_sensitive\\['` equals 3","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v5","material_fingerprint":"7ee75800f3e7f0c1","material_parts":{"children":["647ea2107ca5072f",0],"description":["778fcec0a4875e08",1769],"description_boxes":["6c179f21e6f62b62",0],"file_impact":["5f7d21622afbe78e",1],"ticket_id":["f7810327a51a7548",19]},"metrics":{"cache_read_tokens":101825,"cache_write_tokens":105673,"claim_path":"no-llm/no-network (structural; the fast claim check is a local HMAC verify)","det_ms":9646.6,"input_tokens":230189,"llm_calls":29,"llm_ms":67815.8,"output_tokens":18225,"precheck":{"cited_anchor_warning":false},"total_ms":90578.3,"verify_requests":2},"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5","pr